meta {
  name: CopyController
  seq: 2
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Roles accepted, per access rules §3:

    GET     /copies/statuses          any signed-in user
    GET     /copies/{id}              any signed-in user
    GET     /copies/{id}/qrcode       librarian, admin
    POST    /copies                   librarian, admin
    PUT     /copies/{id}              librarian, admin
    DELETE  /copies/{id}              librarian, admin

  The QR code is a desk tool — it is printed and stuck on the book — which is why the
  one read in this folder that students are refused is that one.

  Not enforced yet: the librarian's libraries. `updateCopy` accepts a `libraryId` and
  moves the copy, so today any librarian can move any copy anywhere, including into
  their own library. That is phase 2 (access rules §4.2).
}
